Reset, instead of accepting, a TCP connection to an IPv6 address from the tun
when keqdroid closes IPv6 there, so the app goes on to its IPv4 address.

On the desktop, with a global IPv6 address on the machine and IPv6 set to
"Block" in the app, keqdroid gives the TUN an IPv6 address, routes ::/0 into it
and closes it with
AND,((IN-TYPE,TUN),(IP-CIDR6,::/0)),REJECT. Rules run after the stack has
answered the SYN, so the app saw a connection open and then close, and Happy
Eyeballs, having settled on IPv6, never tried IPv4: a browser opened no site
at all (complaint of 19.11.2026, there on xray, which got the same fix in
xray-tun-refuse-before-handshake.patch). Before this mihomo let IPv6 go
around the tunnel instead.

keqdroid-tun-close-ipv6: true now makes the tun listener refuse such a SYN
before the handshake, through TCPRejecter from
sing-tun-reject-before-handshake.patch, and the stack answers with a reset, as
a port nobody listens on would. Without the key nothing changes. UDP has no
handshake and is dropped by the rule. On Android keqdroid never writes the
key: there the system closes IPv6 when the VPN has no IPv6 address.

Applies after mihomo-uid-owner-handshake.patch, which brings
RejectTCPBeforeHandshake; the name keeps it sorted after it.

